Fix build on 32-bit x86: WIFI_MTU_SIZE is `#define`d as `(1500UL - 100UL)`,
type `unsigned long`. `size_t` is also `unsigned long` on 64-bit/arm64
(this project's usual targets), so `std::min(WIFI_MTU_SIZE, len - offset)`
resolves there without any cast. On i686 (this container's target),
`size_t` is `unsigned int` - a distinct type from `unsigned long` even
though both are 4 bytes - so template argument deduction for std::min
can't unify the two arguments to one type and fails to compile
(error: no matching function for call to 'min(long unsigned int, size_t)').

---
 src/em/prov/easyconnect/ec_pa_configurator.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/em/prov/easyconnect/ec_pa_configurator.cpp b/src/em/prov/easyconnect/ec_pa_configurator.cpp
--- a/src/em/prov/easyconnect/ec_pa_configurator.cpp
+++ b/src/em/prov/easyconnect/ec_pa_configurator.cpp
@@ -461,7 +461,7 @@
     uint8_t frag_id = 0;

     while (offset < len) {
-        size_t chunk_size = std::min(WIFI_MTU_SIZE, len - offset);
+        size_t chunk_size = std::min(static_cast<size_t>(WIFI_MTU_SIZE), len - offset);

         auto [base_frame, base_len] = ec_util::alloc_gas_frame(dpp_gas_comeback_resp, dialog_token);
